Update the existing **Book Fair 2026 – Match the Author** game. The current connection-line interface is not user-friendly and does not work correctly. Remove the line-drawing system completely and replace it with a simple, reliable drag-and-drop interface.

## Main Game Requirements

Create a single-page matching game with:

* Five author cards
* Five book-cover drop boxes
* Authors and books selected randomly from the complete collection of 20 books
* Authors and books shuffled into different positions
* No login page
* No registration form
* No separate voucher page
* No connection lines

The player must drag each author card and drop it into the box belonging to the correct book.

## Company Theme

Use the attached company image as the visual reference for:

* Company logo
* Primary and secondary colors
* Background colors
* Button colors
* Font style
* Border and card styling
* Overall branding

Do not invent a different theme. Keep the company logo clear and maintain its original proportions.

## Page Layout

### Header

Display:

* Company logo from the attached image
* “Book Fair 2026”
* Game title: “Match the Author”
* Short instruction:
  “Drag each author and drop them onto the correct book.”

### Author Section

Create a clearly labeled box titled:

**Authors**

Inside this box, display five draggable author cards.

Each author card must contain:

* Author name
* Author image, if provided
* Drag icon or visual indicator
* Clear card border
* Touch-friendly size

### Book Section

Create a clearly labeled box titled:

**Books**

Display five book drop boxes in a responsive grid.

Each book box must contain:

* Book-cover image
* Book title
* An empty area labeled:
  “Drop Author Here”

The author and book sections must have separate framed containers so users can easily understand what they need to do.

## Drag-and-Drop Behaviour

The drag-and-drop interaction must work smoothly with:

* Desktop mouse controls
* Laptop touchpads
* Mobile touchscreen controls
* Tablet touchscreen controls

When the player starts dragging an author:

* Slightly enlarge or highlight the author card.
* Highlight all available book drop boxes.
* Display a clear dragging effect.

When the author is dropped onto a book, immediately check the answer.

### Correct Match

If the author matches the book:

* Change the complete book-box frame to green.
* Display a green checkmark.
* Display the text:
  “Correct Match”
* Move the author card into the book box.
* Lock the author and book together.
* Prevent the correctly matched author from being moved again.
* Remove that author from the available Authors section.
* Increase the correct-match count.

### Incorrect Match

If the author does not match the book:

* Change the book-box frame to red.
* Display a red cross icon.
* Display the text:
  “Incorrect Match – Try Again”
* Briefly shake the book box.
* Return the author card to its original position in the Authors section.
* Do not lock the incorrect author into the book box.
* Return the book-box frame to its normal color after approximately two seconds.
* Allow the player to try again.

Do not reveal the correct author after an incorrect attempt.

## Progress Display

Show a simple progress indicator:

**Correct Matches: 0/5**

Update it after every correct match:

* 1/5
* 2/5
* 3/5
* 4/5
* 5/5

Correctly matched books must remain green and locked while the player continues matching the remaining books.

## Winning Condition

The player wins only when all five authors have been correctly dragged onto their matching books.

Required result:

**5 correct matches out of 5**

Do not use a Submit button. Validate each match immediately after the author is dropped.

## Winning Display

When all five matches are correct:

* Stop all further game interaction.
* Keep all five correctly matched book boxes green.
* Show a full-screen celebration animation.
* Add confetti and a smooth success animation.
* Display only the following text:

**Congratulations!**

**You Win a Voucher!**

Do not display:

* The player’s score
* Voucher codes
* Voucher details
* Additional instructions
* Registration forms
* Login forms
* Another page
* Try Again button
* Claim forms
* Extra messages

The final winning display must contain only the congratulations animation and the “You Win a Voucher!” message.

## Random Book Selection

The complete game collection contains 20 books.

For every new game:

1. Randomly select five unique books.
2. Load the correct author for each selected book.
3. Shuffle the five author cards.
4. Shuffle the five book boxes independently.
5. Ensure no duplicate book appears.
6. Ensure no duplicate author appears.
7. Ensure every displayed book has exactly one correct author.

Use only the book covers, titles, author names, author images, and company branding supplied by the administrator. Do not invent any content.

## Responsive Design

### Desktop

* Authors section can appear on the left.
* Books section can appear on the right.
* Display book boxes in a clean grid.

### Mobile and Tablet

* Display the Authors section above the Books section.
* Allow users to drag author cards vertically.
* Automatically scroll the page while dragging near the top or bottom.
* Make book drop boxes large enough for touchscreen use.
* Prevent the page itself from interfering with the drag action.
* Provide tap-to-select and tap-to-drop as a fallback if native dragging is difficult on a mobile device.

For the mobile fallback:

1. Tap an author card to select it.
2. Tap a book box to place the selected author.
3. Apply the same green or red validation behaviour.

## Technical Requirements

Use:

* Next.js
* TypeScript
* Tailwind CSS
* A reliable drag-and-drop library such as `@dnd-kit/core`
* Responsive image components
* Smooth CSS animations
* Confetti animation after winning

Implementation requirements:

* Remove all previous SVG connection-line code.
* Use clear draggable and droppable components.
* Give every author and book a unique ID.
* Validate matches using IDs, not displayed text.
* Prevent duplicate drops.
* Disable a book box after a correct match.
* Disable an author card after a correct match.
* Preserve correct matches if another answer is incorrect.
* Prevent the same author from being placed in multiple books.
* Prevent multiple authors from being locked into the same book.
* Handle missing images with a clean placeholder.
* Keep the interface fast and easy to understand.

## Acceptance Criteria

The updated game is complete when:

1. The entire game works on one page.
2. There are separate framed sections for Authors and Books.
3. Five authors and five book covers are displayed.
4. Author cards can be dragged and dropped onto book boxes.
5. Touchscreen users can select and place authors easily.
6. A correct match immediately changes the complete book frame to green.
7. A correct match displays a green checkmark and “Correct Match.”
8. Correct matches remain locked.
9. An incorrect match immediately changes the book frame to red.
10. An incorrect match displays a red cross and “Incorrect Match – Try Again.”
11. The incorrect author automatically returns to the Authors section.
12. No Submit button is required.
13. Progress updates from 0/5 to 5/5.
14. All five matches must be correct to win.
15. After 5/5 correct matches, a celebration animation appears.
16. The final winning display contains only “Congratulations!” and “You Win a Voucher!”
17. The attached company image is used as the branding and color-theme reference.
18. The game works correctly on desktop, mobile, and tablet devices.

Replace the existing matching interface with this drag-and-drop design. Test every drag, drop, correct-answer, incorrect-answer, mobile-touch, locking, and winning-animation state before considering the game complete.
